          "number": 3,
          "letter": "C",
          "english": "Tiny colleges focus not just on a young person's intellect, but on the young person as a whole. Equally important, tiny colleges ask, \"How can education contribute to human flourishing and the well-being of the world?\" And they shape a college experience to address that question. They replace concerns about institutional growth with attention to the growth of students as fully developed participants in their communities.",
