          "english": "Having just retired from teaching at a public university, I'm now returning to my hometown of Flagstaff, Arizona, to establish a tiny college—Flagstaff College. I'm convinced there's a need for another type of education, one devoted to helping students come into their own and into this beautiful and troubled world. Young people need an education that will provide them with meaning, hope, courage, and passion, as well as information and skills. Large institutions, I believe, are particularly ill-suited to this type of education.",
          "chinese": "刚刚从一所公立大学的教学岗位上退休，我现在正回到家乡亚利桑那州弗拉格斯塔夫，创办一所微型学院——弗拉格斯塔夫学院。我确信，我们需要另一种教育，一种致力于帮助学生充分发展自我、走进这个美丽而又充满困扰的世界的教育。年轻人需要的教育，不仅要为他们提供信息和技能，还要赋予他们意义、希望、勇气和热情。在我看来，大型机构尤其不适合开展这种教育。",
