          "number": 7,
          "letter": "G",
          "english": "With only 26 students, Deep Springs is the smallest college in the country and, quite likely, the most atypical(非典型的). Located on a working cattle ranch on the California-Nevada border, Deep Springs is a private, residential, two-year college for men, committed to educating students for \"a life of service to humanity.\" Founded by the electricity tycoon(大亨) L.L. Nunn in 1917, Deep Springs \"curriculum\" revolves around academics, labor, and self-governance. In addition to their courses, students are charged with running the 155-acre ranch and overseeing the functioning of the college. Students chair both the admissions and the curriculum committees.",
          "chinese": "深泉学院只有26名学生，是全国规模最小、很可能也是最非典型的学院。它坐落在加利福尼亚州与内华达州交界处的一座正在经营的牧牛场上，是一所私立寄宿制两年制男子学院，致力于培养学生“为人类服务的一生”。深泉学院由电力大亨L.L. Nunn于1917年创办，其“课程”围绕学业、劳动和自我管理展开。除了学习课程之外，学生还负责经营这座155英亩的牧场，并监督学院的运转。招生委员会和课程委员会均由学生担任主席。",
