          "number": 14,
          "letter": "N",
          "english": "The ultimate justification for a tiny college is the conviction that each of us comes into our full humanity by close interaction with those who know and care for us, and that one of the basic purposes of higher education is social. Although we give lip service to the idea that a college education will make us better people, when all's said and done, we think of higher education primarily in economic terms. We've come to think of higher education as a means to make a living rather than make a life. We've also come to see higher education as a private good rather than a public one. Tiny colleges are not the answer to all of our educational requirements, but they're an answer to one of our most basic educational necessities; the need to produce thoughtful, engaged, and compassionate human beings.",
          "chinese": "支持创办微型学院的最终理由，是坚信我们每个人都要通过与那些了解并关心我们的人密切互动，才能充分实现自身的人性；而高等教育的基本目的之一就是社会性目的。尽管我们口头上赞同大学教育会使我们成为更好的人，但归根结底，我们主要还是从经济角度看待高等教育。我们逐渐把高等教育视为谋生的手段，而不是创造生活的途径。我们也逐渐把高等教育看成一种私人利益，而非公共利益。微型学院并不能解决我们所有的教育需求，但它能够满足我们最基本的教育需要之一：培养有思想、积极参与社会且富有同情心的人。",
